(An orphan process is a child whose parent terminated without waiting for it; the Linux init process \(PID 1\) automatically) Tj
T* (adopts orphan processes and reaps their exit status. A zombie process is a process that has completed execution via exit\(\),) Tj
T* (but its parent has not yet called wait\(\) to read its exit code; its PCB remains in the process table, consuming PID slots.) Tj
ET
